From d4b343221843352043927aba8f85575c484e16c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yi-sudo <skyockqq38@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:14:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Batch decode: one launch for all rows in QSA attention and
 GDN recurrence (opt-in)

With --batch N the verify window ran QSA block scoring, top-k and decode
attention as one launch per row, and the GDN recurrence (window and 1-row
commit) as one launch per slot.  At 4-8 live slots these serial launches are
most of the window's cost beyond the expert reads.

Two env switches, both off by default (off = the same launches as before):

  STRATA_BATCH_ATTN_ROWS=1   block scores, top-k and decode attention for all
                             rows of the window in one launch each; every row
                             reads its own slot's indexer keys and K/V pools
                             (passed by value as kernel params, so the graph
                             captured per row layout stays valid).  A slot that
                             streams KV (kv_mode 1) keeps the per-row path.
  STRATA_BATCH_GDN_GROUPS=1  GDN recurrence in the window and the 1-row commit
                             for all slots in one launch (grid.y = slot group).
                             Conv commits stay per slot.

Same arithmetic per row: 4 concurrent temperature-0 prompts give the same
bytes with and without the switches (--batch 4 and --batch 8).

RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell, IQ3_S, all experts in VRAM, a0116b2, same day,
total tok/s (docs/BATCHING.md has the table):
  --batch 4, 4 clients: 268.4 -> 311.7
  --batch 8, 8 clients: 308.4 -> 374.8 (reserve 6144 MiB)
Window: 4 rows 14.3 -> 12.2 ms, 8 rows 24.6 -> 19.9 ms.

Built and run with CUDA 13.0 (sm_120) only.  The .cu files are also in the
HIP build, which was not built here (no ROCm).  The SYCL port has its own
copies of these files and is untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
